In <repo>, branch feat/wire-verifysignature (PR #252, already open): fix one Copilot review finding.

File: internal/daemon/config.go, in `(*Config) ResolveOwnerKeyID`. The final check:

```go
if !fingerprintPattern.MatchString(keyID) {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("daemon owner key %q is not a full 40-hex OpenPGP fingerprint", keyID)
}
```

Copilot's finding: this error doesn't say whether the bad fingerprint came from `owner_gpg_key_id` directly or from the `owner_handle`-resolved identity's `gpg_key_id` — makes operator debugging harder when daemon.json is misconfigured. Fix by tailoring the error message to name the actual source: when the switch's `case c.OwnerHandle != "":` branch resolved `keyID`, a malformed result should say something like `owner identity %q's gpg_key_id %q is not a full 40-hex OpenPGP fingerprint` (naming the handle); when the `case c.OwnerGPGKeyID != "":` branch resolved it, say `daemon owner_gpg_key_id %q is not a full 40-hex OpenPGP fingerprint` (naming the config field directly). Keep the exact same validation behavior (same fingerprintPattern check, same control flow) — only the error message needs to become source-specific. Update internal/daemon/config_test.go's existing malformed-fingerprint test cases ("owner_gpg_key_id malformed", "owner_handle malformed fingerprint in extension") to assert against the new, more specific substrings if the current `wantErrSub` assertions no longer match.

Run `make check` after, commit with a message like `fix(daemon): name the config source in ResolveOwnerKeyID's malformed-fingerprint error`, and push to the existing branch (git push, no -u needed, it already tracks origin). Report back when done.

